Package: hd-buildserver
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, git, make, openssh-client, passwd, systemd, hd-docker, hd-base (>= 1.22)
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian build server
 Builds HyprDebian from its git repository every night and updates a
 HyprDebian package repository of hd-repo with it. When the branch has moved
 since the last build, or Debian has a new kernel or ZFS for the kernels of
 hd-kernel, it checks out its head in a clean checkout, builds every package
 and the live ISO in a clean debian:trixie container, and uploads the
 packages that are not in the repository yet and the ISO. The kernels come
 from a cache when they were built of the same versions before.
 .
 The git repository, the branch and the host name of the package repository
 are the key hd-buildserver in /etc/hyprdebian/config.json. The build runs as
 the user hd-buildserver, which may run docker; its ssh key, generated on the
 first installation, goes in the authorized_keys of the user repo of the
 package repository. Installing the package enables hd-buildserver.timer.
